the main conclusion of this afternoon  session was that we stand fully resolved  that we will always stand for our values  Europe has been under attack before but  we've always defended Liberty democracy  and we will do that we'll do that  together for that we adopted a  declaration in the afternoon which  emphasizes that we will exchange  information even swifter than we already  do that we will now very soon need to  implement the passenger named records we  will need to see a swift completion of  legislation on combating terrorism so we  don't need new plans we need to fully  execute the plans that have been the  measures that have been taken before and  decided upon before and the strong  result of the meeting is afternoon ones  to do that all European ministers the  Commission and European Parliament  together with us insisted on the swift  acting of the European institutions on  the different points of action of our  joint declaration and I only would like  to underline several some points of it  which are really in our view in the  Belgian view very important that is  first the interoperability of databases  which is really necessary would regard  to for instance the Schengen information  system but with regard to a lot of  example given Interpol databases we  really have to act swiftly on that issue  another issue which was very important  is the full exchange of judicial  information every day we discover in the  framework of what happened in bearers  and in Brussels how important it is that  our intelligence services that our  judicial services exchange all relevant  information that is required this  terrible this horrendous attacks cannot  continue to be wake-up calls forever we  owe this to our citizens all of them so  what  do we need to do in the coming days in  the coming weeks to prevent as much as  possible this type of events to happen  again two essential elements first  improve on our exchange of information  and second implement put in practice  what was politically agreed after  previous attacks remember from last  December our agreement on PNR why is it  still in place parliament has to vote to  adopt it and this has to happen now to  those that wish to divide us we respond  with unity resilience and determination  as our meeting demonstrates today and  this is a very strong message we want to  send from this meeting because it is  what we stand for as Europeans
 

